5.3.3 Types of models
In terms of the taxonomy of the proposed GNN models, 6 out of 16 papers utilize attentional GNNs, 9 papers employ convolutional GNNs, and one paper takes into account both convolutional and attentional GNNs (Ref. [69]). As for the graph structure, some papers use models which learn the graph structure themselves (e.g., Refs. [292, 177, 162, 237, 33]), whereas some others define it a priori, based on the relationships between companies and stocks (e.g., Refs. [312, 120, 357, 364]). Half of the papers deal with a stock movement classification problem, so the most commonly used loss function is cross entropy. The majority of the papers explicitly indicate that Python is the programming language utilized, with nearly half employing PyTorch, and a few utilizing TensorFlow. Only Refs. [312] and [237] provide a link to the source code of the proposed models, which are, respectively, the knowledge graph with graph convolution neural network (KG-GCN) model, available at https://github.com/Gjl12321/KG GCN Stock Price Trend Prediction System, and the spectral temporal graph neural network (StemGNN), available at https://github.com/cevher/Time-Series-A nalysis.
